{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem he succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. \n*Early Life* \nhe was a member of the House of Toulouse and played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states in the 12th century. \n*Family and Succession* \nhe was married to Hodierna of Jerusalem's niece also named Hodierna and had no children with her after her death he married a woman named Bourgogne but had no children with her either. \n*Crusades and Military Campaigns* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was a skilled military leader and fought in several battles against the Muslim forces led by Saladin and Nur ad-Din he was also a key figure in the Battle of Inab in 1149 where the Crusader forces were defeated. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was taken prisoner by the Muslim forces in 1164 and was held captive for several years he was eventually released and returned to Tripoli where he continued to rule as Count until his death in 1187. \n*Later Life and Death* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli played an important role in the politics of the Crusader states and was a key figure in the negotiations between the Crusader leaders and the Muslim forces he was also a patron of the arts and architecture and commissioned several building projects in Tripoli. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187 and was succeeded by his nephew Raymond IV Count of Tripoli his death marked the end of an era in the history of the Crusader states and had significant consequences for the future of the region. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was remembered as a brave and skilled military leader who fought to defend the Crusader states against the Muslim forces his legacy continued to shape the history of the region for centuries after his death. \nThe history of Raymond III Count of Tripoli is well documented in historical records and provides valuable insights into the politics and society of the Crusader states in the 12th century. \n*Historical Records* \nthe life and reign of Raymond III Count of Tripoli is an important part of the history of the Crusades and continues to be studied by historians and scholars today. \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was a complex figure who played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states his life and reign continue to fascinate historians and scholars and provide valuable insights into the politics and society of the medieval Middle East.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015948931104503572}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.8347842693328857}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.48570793867111206}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -3.933898824470816e-06}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.06854468584060669}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0001662831346038729}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -0.0001380348257953301}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -0.0017091918271034956}, {"token": "erna", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": -0.0003094194398727268}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.03004475310444832}, {"token": " succeeded", "logprob": -0.5372155904769897}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " father", "logprob": -3.814689989667386e-06}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.06210620701313019}, {"t